UID:48194eb03a631ccf@nutcracker2026
DTSTAMP:20260914T010516Z
SEQUENCE:2026091401
DTSTART;TZID=America/Chicago:20261210T180000
DTEND;TZID=America/Chicago:20261210T194500
SUMMARY:Nutcracker: Cast B Dress Rehearsal – ACT I Cast B (Mandatory 
 – Production Week)
LOCATION:Robinson Center
DESCRIPTION:Thu. Dec. 10 · Call 6:00 PM · 7:00 PM–7:45 PM · Robinson
  Center\nMANDATORY — production week. CALL TIME 6:00 PM: dancers must 
 be checked in and backstage by then\, so arrive by 5:45 PM. BA: Call Tim
 e is the time dancers should be check-in and backstage - Arrive 15 minut
 es before Call Time.\nACT I Dress Run\; In Performance Costumes\, Hair a
 nd Makeup.\nAll Casts are called unless a cast is named. SUBJECT TO CHAN
 GE — the BA master schedule\, the weekly BA emails and the BA portal a
 re the official source. Master: https://docs.google.com/spreadsheets/d/1
 xWFCPfY5m0aK9d5dnxvALNre-6-N7Cl0kkw24rvm6cE/\n\nCOSTUME / HAIR / MAKEUP 
 for Party Children: Party Children — Costume (you provide): Pink Seaml
 ess Tights\, Flesh-tone camisole leotard Male: Black Tights\; Shoes: Pin
 k Ballet Shoes\, no ribbons Male: Black Ballet Shoes\; Makeup: Light Sta
 ge Makeup\; Hair: Half Up-Half Down\, Curls (natural or curled) Male: Ne
 at and out of the eyes\; Accessories (BA provides): Hair Bows Male: N/A\
 ; Prop (BA provides): Dolls/Hobby Horse\nLight Stage Makeup Instruction 
 Sheet:\n•  Powder matching skintone\n•  Light brown eye shadow
  applied to the crease with an eye shadow brush\n•  Dark Brown/Blac
 k eyeliner and black mascara. No fake lashes.\n•  Blush on the chee
 ks (be sure to apply plenty so dancer doesn’t look washed out in the s
 tage lights)\n•  Red or Dark Red lipstick\nDancers of Color may wea
 r flesh tone tights and flesh tone ballet shoes.\nCostume Care Guideline
 s:\n•  Handle costume pieces with care while changing to prevent da
 mage to delicate fabrics\n•  Promptly notify Ballet Arkansas in the
  event of costume damage at the point of discovery\, no matter how signi
 ficant\n•  Never throw costumes or accessories on the floor\, or ha
 ng costumes by their elastic straps\n•  Refrain from sitting on the
  floor while in costume\n•  Do not attempt to alter\, mend\, clean\
 , or launder any costume or accessory\n•  Never apply stage make-up
  while in costume and shall take great care to refrain from smudging mak
 e-up on costume during its removal\n•  Refrain from the use of spra
 y perfume or cologne while in costume\n•  Never wear any garment no
 t assigned to cast member\n•  Do not handle or consume food or beve
 rage while in costume\, with the exception of water\n•  Do not remo
 ve costumes from their assigned dressing rooms or from the theater\n• 
  Remove all bobby pins used to secure head pieces and wigs following 
 their use\n•  Return all headpieces to their assigned bags\n• 
  Comply fully with any and all updates to Ballet Arkansas’ wardrobe po
 licies\n•  Do not pack markers\, paints\, colored drinks or anythin
 g that may damage or stain costumes.
BEGIN:VALARM
TRIGGER:-PT1H
ACTION:DISPLAY
DESCRIPTION:Nutcracker in 1 hour
END:VALARM
END:VEVENT
